# llvm, target libclc: the OpenCL C library of LLVM, what Mesa needs for rusticl. Since LLVM 23 it is a
# runtime built with the just built clang, which the cross build cannot run: the SPIR-V it produces is
# target independent, so it is built in the sources of the package with the clang of lfs/llvm:native
# and the llvm-spirv of the cross translator (postbuild.sh)
### Not the default build: the values of package.env this target keeps or drops
PKG_DEPS="lfs/llvm:native lfs/Vulkan-SPIRV-LLVM-Translator:cross"
BUILD_PROCESS=none
